9. Retry

Retry is useful for transient failures.

java
@Retry(
    name = "paymentService",
    fallbackMethod = "fallback"
)
public PaymentResponse pay(PaymentRequest request) {
    return paymentClient.pay(request);
}

But **never blindly retry everything**.

For example:

POST /payment

If payment actually succeeded but response was lost, retrying may charge the customer twice.

Therefore use **idempotency**.

Idempotency-Key: abc-123

Payment service stores:

abc-123 → SUCCESS

and returns the existing result for repeated requests.


