18. PostgreSQL Partitioning

Suppose you have:

transactions

500 million records

Instead of one giant table:

transactions

partition by date:

transactions
 ├── transactions_2026_01
 ├── transactions_2026_02
 ├── transactions_2026_03
 └── transactions_2026_04

Example:

sql
CREATE TABLE transactions (
    id BIGSERIAL,
    created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
    amount NUMERIC
) PARTITION BY RANGE (created_at);

Then:

sql
CREATE TABLE transactions_2026_08
PARTITION OF transactions
FOR VALUES FROM ('2026-08-01')
TO ('2026-09-01');

Advantages:

- smaller indexes
- partition pruning
- easier archival
- improved maintenance


