24. Kafka Partitioning

Suppose:

order-events

Partition 0
Partition 1
Partition 2

Producer:

orderId = 100

Kafka uses the key:

hash(orderId) % partitions

This ensures events with the same key generally go to the same partition.

Therefore:

Order 100 CREATED
Order 100 PAID
Order 100 SHIPPED

can preserve ordering within that partition.


25. Kafka Consumer Group

Suppose:

Topic
 ├── P0
 ├── P1
 └── P2

Consumer group:

Payment Group
 ├── Consumer 1 → P0
 ├── Consumer 2 → P1
 └── Consumer 3 → P2

Another group:

Analytics Group
 ├── Consumer 1 → P0
 ├── Consumer 2 → P1
 └── Consumer 3 → P2

Each consumer group gets its own logical copy of the messages.


26. Kafka Offset

Consumer tracks:

offset = 105

Meaning it has processed messages up to a certain position.

If consumer crashes:

restart
   ↓
read committed offset
   ↓
continue

This is fundamental to Kafka reliability.


