The key senior-level mindset

For this position, don't answer technologies independently.

Instead, think:

> **How do I build a reliable, scalable, secure, observable distributed system using these technologies?**

For example, if asked about Kafka, don't stop at:

> "Kafka is a distributed messaging system."

Say:

> "I'd use Kafka/MSK when I need durable asynchronous communication and independent consumers. I'd partition by a business key when ordering matters, use consumer groups for horizontal scalability, monitor consumer lag, handle retries/DLQs, make consumers idempotent, and consider the outbox pattern when publishing events alongside database transactions."

That kind of answer is what separates a **Senior Backend Engineer** from someone who has simply memorized technology definitions.